-- title:
--   FM pointwise products by recursive calls
-- statement:
--   Let `pF` satisfy `FMSpec pF iprog I n C`: calling it multiplies any $a,b\in[0,2^n]$ modulo $F=2^n+1$ (given `PRM`$=n$, `RN`$=2^n$, `RF`$=F$ on top) within cost $C$. Let $A,B$ be lists of equal length of canonical residues mod $F$, with the bit length of $|A|$ at most $n$. Assume `V` holds $A$ over $R_V$, `DX` holds $B$ over $R_X$, `DL` has $|A|$ on top, and `PRM`, `RN`, `RF` hold $n$, $2^n$, $F$ on top. Then `fmPw pF` runs from $s$ to the state where `V`$=R_V$, `DX`$=R_X$, and the products
--   $$\mathrm{pmulZ}(F,A,B) = \big((a_i b_i)\bmod F\big)_i$$
--   are pushed onto `P1` in reverse order (last on top), with cost at most
--   $$|A|\,\big(C+2000(n+3)+30\big)+1000(n+3).$$
--
--   This is the only place where the procedure recurses: the $K=2^k$ pointwise products of the transformed sequences are computed by $K$ calls of `FM` at the smaller size, which yields the term $2^k C$ in `fmMain_runs`.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** States are `IState NS` records with item stacks `G : Fin NS → List Item` (head = top), input pointer `ip` and output `out`; `s.upd X L` replaces stack `X` by `L`; `ints A` is the list of integer items of `A`. The named stacks (`ARG`, `PRM`, `RN`, `RF`, `DX`, `DL`, …) are fixed indices in `Fin 32`. `IRuns I iprog p s s' c` means that `p` executes from `s` to exactly `s'` with some cost $c' \le c$, so costs are upper bounds; the program text `iprog` and input `I` are arbitrary unless constrained. `FMSpec` is a hypothesis about the procedure `pF`, discharged by induction on $N$ in the final proof.
-- source:
--   A. Schönhage, V. Strassen, Schnelle Multiplikation großer Zahlen, Computing 7 (1971), 281–292 (main theorem: O(n log n log log n) multitape TM multiplication). Lemma `NLogN.fmPw_runs` of the Lean development NLogN/SSFM2.lean (lines 78–136), written for the prove2.me integer-multiplication campaign.

-- Schönhage–Strassen multitape-TM development (NLogN), generated by skeleton subtraction.

import Definitions.Def_IntMul_SS_Defs2

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false
set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000

open NLogN
open IntMul
variable {P : ℕ} {I : List Sym} {iprog : Fin P → IStmt NS P}

theorem NLogN.fmPw_runs (pF : Fin P) (n C : ℕ) (hFM : FMSpec pF iprog I n C) (s : IState NS)
    (A B : List ℤ) (RV RX LL LP LN LF : List Item) (hl : A.length = B.length)
    (hzK : zsz (A.length : ℤ) ≤ n) (hA : Canon (2 ^ n + 1) A) (hB : Canon (2 ^ n + 1) B)
    (hV : s.G V = ints A ++ RV) (hX : s.G DX = ints B ++ RX) (hL : s.G DL = .int A.length :: LL)
    (hP : s.G PRM = .int n :: LP) (hN : s.G RN = .int (2 ^ n) :: LN)
    (hF : s.G RF = .int (2 ^ n + 1) :: LF) :
    IRuns I iprog (fmPw pF) s
      (((s.upd V RV).upd DX RX).upd P1 ((ints (pmulZ (2 ^ n + 1) A B)).reverse ++ s.G P1))
      (A.length * (C + 2000 * (n + 3) + 30) + 1000 * (n + 3)) := by sorry
